---
title: Collection and Identification
sidebar:
  label: Collection and identification
  order: 3
---

The `Collection & Identification` card stores the core specimen metadata, in
this order on screen:

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Specimen UUID` | Unique identifier assigned by NAHPU; read-only and selectable. |
| `Museum ID` | Optional museum catalog or accession number. Shown after `Show more`, or once it has a value. |
| `Field ID` | The cataloger's field number or a formatted project number. Select the edit icon to open `Edit field ID` and switch between `Personnel` and `Project`; NAHPU asks you to confirm, removes the previous identifier, and does not reuse numbers already taken. |
| `Cataloger` | The person who catalogs the specimen (from personnel with the `Cataloger` role). Choosing one also sets `Preparator` and `Determiner`. |
| `Preparator` | The person who prepared the specimen or voucher (`Cataloger` or `Preparator only` roles). |
| `Condition` | The specimen's condition, from the `Conditions` controlled vocabulary in `Settings`. |
| `Collection date`, `Collection time` | When the specimen was collected. |
| `Prep. date`, `Prep. time` | When the specimen was prepared. |

The **Identification** section of the card holds:

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Taxon` | A record from the project's taxon registry. |
| `Determiner` | The person who identified the specimen (`Cataloger` or `Determiner only` roles). |
| `ID Confidence` | `High`, `Medium`, `Low`, or `Not assigned`. |
| `Identification Method` | Optional evidence used, from the `Identification Methods` controlled vocabulary. Appears once `ID Confidence` is set. |

## Taxonomy

The `Taxon Info` card reads from the taxon selected in `Collection & Identification`.
On the specimen form it displays `Class`, `Order`, and `Family`. Select
`View details` to review the full read-only taxonomy record:

- **Header**: scientific name, `Authors`, and `Common name` when present.
- **Classification**: `Rank`, `Kingdom` and `Phylum` (taken from the registry
  when recorded, or inferred from class otherwise), `Class`, `Order`, `Family`,
  `Genus`, and — when applicable — `Species`, `Subspecies`, and `Authors`.
- **Conservation**: `Red List category`, `CITES status`, and `Country status`
  when present, plus `Notes`.
- **Total records & sharing**: record counts for `Current project` and
  `All projects`, and a `Taxon QR code` to share the taxon.
